  "text": {
    "en": {
      "title": "Basel Framework: MAR21.58 FAQ1 vs MAR21.33(1)",
      "summary": "The CTP index FAQ says 'at least 75%' while citing MAR21.33(1), which says 'more than 75%'; exactly 75% gets two different buckets.",
      "impact": "Position: Credit index CTP, constituents by weight: exactly 75% IG financials (bucket 3) and 25% other; CS01 = 100,000. Reading a: FAQ: at least 75% -> bucket 3, RW (Table 6) 8.0%, WS = 8,000. Reading b: MAR21.33(1): not more than 75% -> fallback (bucket 16, 13.0%) WS = 13,000. Difference: WS 5,000",
      "correction": "Clarify or correct the cited passage so that the rule and its references give one result for the stated case."
    }
  },
